# Requests for every endpoint and every error situation.
#
# Works with the REST Client extension in VS Code and with Visual Studio / Rider (2024.3+).
# Requests marked "# @name" can be referenced by later requests, e.g. {{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}},
# so run them from top to bottom within a section.
#
# Watch the API's log output while you run these: every response carries a traceId that matches a log line.

@root_url = http://localhost:8080
@portland_brewery = 936c3d7e-5d54-4459-b72c-117cdda059b4
@portland_brewery_2 = 45249b6e-b1d0-4c2f-a60e-ab483169287f
@closed_brewery = 08155729-56b6-4a82-a43e-5b458dd01c2e
@san_diego_brewery = 5fdcc498-f9df-4fa5-b35d-487a59f0fecc


###############################################################################
# Basics
###############################################################################

### Health check
GET {{root_url}}/health

### OpenAPI document (the Scalar UI is at /scalar)
GET {{root_url}}/openapi/v1.json

### Reset the database to the seed data
POST {{root_url}}/admin/reset


###############################################################################
# Error catalog: every errorCode the API can return
###############################################################################

### All error codes
GET {{root_url}}/errors

### One error code (this is what the "type" URI in a ProblemDetails points to)
GET {{root_url}}/errors/crawl.version_mismatch

### 404 error.not_found: unknown error code
GET {{root_url}}/errors/does.not_exist


###############################################################################
# Breweries (read only, no user needed)
# The X-Data-Source response header says where the data came from: live, cache or snapshot.
###############################################################################

### List breweries
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries

### Filter and page
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?city=portland&type=brewpub&page=1&perPage=5

### Search by name
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?name=breakside

### Get one brewery
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries/{{portland_brewery}}

### 404 brewery.not_found
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries/no-such-brewery

### 400 validation.failed: one field wrong (see "errors" and "errorCodes")
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?type=winery

### 400 validation.failed: several fields wrong at once
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?type=winery&page=0&perPage=500

### 400 request.malformed: page is not a number
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?page=two


###############################################################################
# Crawls: reading (no user needed)
###############################################################################

### List crawls (oldest first)
# @name crawls
GET {{root_url}}/api/crawls

### Filter by city
GET {{root_url}}/api/crawls?city=portland

### Get one crawl (the ETag header holds its version)
GET {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{crawls.response.body.$[0].id}}

### 404 crawl.not_found
GET {{root_url}}/api/crawls/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 404 request.not_found: the id is not a guid, so no route matches
GET {{root_url}}/api/crawls/not-a-guid


###############################################################################
# Crawls: the happy path
# Users are faked with the X-User header. alice and bob own the seed crawls, but any name works.
###############################################################################

### Create a crawl
# @name myCrawl
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
X-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Workshop warm-up",
  "city": "Portland",
  "date": "2030-06-01"
}

### Get it
GET {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}

### Add a stop, using the ETag from when we created it
# @name addStop
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops
X-User: alice
If-Match: {{myCrawl.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "{{portland_brewery}}"
}

### Add another stop, using the ETag from the previous change
# @name addStop2
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops
X-User: alice
If-Match: {{addStop.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "{{portland_brewery_2}}"
}

### Rename it
# @name renamed
PUT {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}
X-User: alice
If-Match: {{addStop2.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Workshop warm-up (renamed)",
  "date": "2030-06-02"
}

### Remove a stop
DELETE {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops/{{portland_brewery_2}}
X-User: alice


###############################################################################
# Crawls: errors
# Run "Create a crawl" above first. Most of these use that crawl.
# Rejected requests also count toward the rate limit on creating crawls, so the bad creates below use different users.
###############################################################################

### 401 auth.unauthenticated: no X-User header
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Anonymous crawl",
  "city": "Portland",
  "date": "2030-06-01"
}

### 401 auth.unauthenticated: invalid user name
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
X-User: not a valid name!
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Crawl",
  "city": "Portland",
  "date": "2030-06-01"
}

### 403 crawl.not_owner: bob tries to rename alice's crawl
PUT {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}
X-User: bob
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob was here",
  "date": "2030-06-01"
}

### 412 crawl.version_mismatch: the ETag from when the crawl was created is out of date by now
PUT {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}
X-User: alice
If-Match: {{myCrawl.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Overwriting someone else's change",
  "date": "2030-06-01"
}

### 409 crawl.duplicate_stop: the brewery is already a stop
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops
X-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "{{portland_brewery}}"
}

### 422 crawl.brewery_wrong_city: a San Diego brewery on a Portland crawl
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops
X-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "{{san_diego_brewery}}"
}

### 422 crawl.brewery_not_open: the brewery has closed
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops
X-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "{{closed_brewery}}"
}

### 422 crawl.unknown_brewery: the brewery is in the body, not the URL, so this is 422 and not 404
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops
X-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "no-such-brewery"
}

### 422 crawl.in_the_past: alice's seed crawl from last summer can't be changed
# (Run "GET /api/crawls" in the reading section first: the oldest crawl is listed first.)
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{crawls.response.body.$[0].id}}/stops
X-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "{{portland_brewery_2}}"
}

### 404 crawl.stop_not_found
DELETE {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops/no-such-brewery
X-User: alice

### 400 validation.failed: missing and too long fields, date in the past
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
X-User: dave
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "city": "Portlandddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd",
  "date": "2020-01-01"
}

### 400 request.malformed: broken JSON
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
X-User: erin
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Missing the closing brace"

### 400 request.malformed: date in the wrong format
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
X-User: frank
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Crawl",
  "city": "Portland",
  "date": "01.06.2030"
}

### 415 http.415: not JSON
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
X-User: grace
Content-Type: text/plain

Just some text

### 405 request.method_not_allowed: PATCH is not supported
PATCH {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}
X-User: alice
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 429 request.rate_limited: send this 4 times within a minute (the limit is 3 new crawls per user per minute)
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls
X-User: carol
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Spam crawl",
  "city": "Portland",
  "date": "2030-06-01"
}


###############################################################################
# Chaos: simulate failures with the X-Chaos header (or ?chaos=). Combine modes with commas.
###############################################################################

### 500 server.unexpected: the API itself fails
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries
X-Chaos: fail

### Slow response (5 seconds): try a loading spinner, or cancel the request
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries
X-Chaos: slow

### Flaky: fails half of the time, so try a retry in the frontend
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries
X-Chaos: flaky

### Chaos as a query parameter instead of a header
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?chaos=fail

### 400: unknown chaos mode
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries
X-Chaos: explode

### Open Brewery DB is down, but we fall back to the snapshot: 200 with X-Data-Source: snapshot
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?city=san diego
X-Chaos: upstream-down

### 502 upstream.unavailable: Open Brewery DB is down and fallback is disabled
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?city=san diego
X-Chaos: upstream-down, no-fallback

### 504 upstream.timeout: Open Brewery DB doesn't answer in time (takes a few seconds)
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?city=san diego
X-Chaos: upstream-timeout, no-fallback

### 503 upstream.circuit_open: we've stopped calling Open Brewery DB for a while
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries?city=san diego
X-Chaos: upstream-circuit-open, no-fallback

### Upstream failure while changing data: adding a stop also looks up the brewery
POST {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}/stops
X-User: alice
X-Chaos: upstream-down, no-fallback
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "breweryId": "{{san_diego_brewery}}"
}

### Not JSON-friendly client: errors are still JSON, even when asking for HTML
GET {{root_url}}/api/breweries
Accept: text/html
X-Chaos: fail


###############################################################################
# Clean up
###############################################################################

### Delete the crawl
DELETE {{root_url}}/api/crawls/{{myCrawl.response.body.$.id}}
X-User: alice
